# Kconfig for trackball 15-degree rotation input processor + behavior

config ZMK_INPUT_PROCESSOR_ROTATE
    bool "Rotate trackball movement in 15-degree steps"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_POINTING
    depends on INPUT
    help
      Enables an input processor that rotates relative X/Y pointer
      movement in 24 discrete 15-degree steps. The current step is
      shared global state, adjustable at runtime via the
      zmk,behavior-rotate-step behavior.

config ZMK_BEHAVIOR_ROTATE_STEP
    bool "Behavior to adjust trackball rotation angle at runtime"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_INPUT_PROCESSOR_ROTATE
    help
      Enables a keymap behavior that steps the trackball rotation
      angle by +-15 degrees (param1 = +1 for clockwise, -1 for
      counter-clockwise) each time it is pressed.
